==English==

===Etymology===
{{m|en|split}} + {{m|en|end}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# A [[hair]] which has split at the end, usually from dryness or innutrition. ''(Usually in plural)''
#: ''I've got so many '''split ends''' – I think I must be working too hard.''
# {{lb|en|American football}} The position which lines up wide and on the [[offensive line of scrimmage]] whose primary job is to serve as a receiver.
#: ''Jones played '''split end'''.''
# {{lb|en|American football}} A player playing the position of split end.
#: ''The '''split end''' ran deep.''

